{
  "id": "metals_and_alloys___young_s_modulus_of_elasticity",
  "title": "Metals and Alloys - Young's Modulus of Elasticity",
  "description": "Elastic properties and Young's modulus for metals and alloys like cast iron, carbon steel and more. Calculate Young's modulus of elasticity (E) for various metals and alloys at different temperatures.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Young's Modulus of Elasticity Calculator\n\nYoung's modulus (E) is the ratio of stress to strain and represents the elasticity of a material. It can be used to predict elongation or compression of an object.\n\n**Unit Conversion:**\n- 1 psi (lb/in²) = 6,894.8 Pa (N/m²)\n- T (°C) = 5/9 × (T (°F) - 32)\n\nThis tool provides Young's modulus values for common metals and alloys at various temperatures according to ASME B31.1-1995."
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Metal/Alloy Type",
        "Temperature (°C)",
        "Young's Modulus (10⁶ psi)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Gray cast iron",
          "-200 to 538",
          "13.4 to 10.2"
        ],
        [
          "Carbon steel C ≤ 0.3%",
          "-200 to 649",
          "31.4 to 18.0"
        ],
        [
          "Carbon steel C ≥ 0.3%",
          "-200 to 649",
          "31.2 to 15.4"
        ],
        [
          "Carbon-molybdenum steels",
          "-200 to 649",
          "31.1 to 15.3"
        ],
        [
          "Nickel steels Ni 2%-9%",
          "-200 to 482",
          "29.6 to 23.0"
        ],
        [
          "Cr-Mo steels Cr 1/2%-2%",
          "-200 to 649",
          "31.6 to 21.8"
        ],
        [
          "Cr-Mo steels Cr 2.25%-3%",
          "-200 to 649",
          "32.6 to 22.5"
        ],
        [
          "Cr-Mo steels Cr 5%-9%",
          "-200 to 649",
          "32.9 to 18.2"
        ],
        [
          "Chromium steels Cr 12%, 17%, 27%",
          "-200 to 649",
          "31.2 to 16.6"
        ],
        [
          "Austenitic steels (TP304, 310, 316, 321, 347)",
          "-200 to 649",
          "30.3 to 21.2"
        ],
        [
          "Copper (C11000)",
          "-200 to 538",
          "16.9 to 13.7"
        ],
        [
          "Naval brass Si & Al bronze",
          "-200 to 538",
          "15.9 to 12.8"
        ],
        [
          "Comp. and leaded-Sn bronze",
          "-200 to 538",
          "14.8 to 12.0"
        ],
        [
          "Copper red brass Al-bronze",
          "-200 to 538",
          "18.0 to 14.5"
        ],
        [
          "Monel 400 (N04400)",
          "-200 to 649",
          "27.8 to 21.2"
        ],
        [
          "Unalloyed titanium (Gr. 1,2,3,7)",
          "-200 to 427",
          "15.5 to 11.2"
        ],
        [
          "Aluminum alloys (443, 1060, 1100, 3003, 3004, 6063)",
          "-200 to 482",
          "11.1 to 8.7"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "temperature_celsius",
          "label": "Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 20,
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "material_modulus",
          "label": "Young's Modulus at Reference Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 30,
          "unit": "10⁶ psi"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "modulus_psi",
          "label": "Young's Modulus",
          "formula": "inputs.material_modulus",
          "unit": "10⁶ psi",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "modulus_pa",
          "label": "Young's Modulus",
          "formula": "inputs.material_modulus * 6894.8",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "scientific"
        },
        {
          "id": "modulus_mpa",
          "label": "Young's Modulus",
          "formula": "inputs.material_modulus * 6.8948",
          "unit": "MPa",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}